    5815	### D45 — Baker-Norine graph Riemann-Roch / chip-firing rank of the prime divisor on an arithmetic graph
    5816	
    5817	**Question:** Baker-Norine 2007 *Adv. Math.* 215, 766 = arXiv:math/0608360
    5818	prove a graph-theoretic Riemann-Roch theorem: for any finite connected
    5819	graph `G` and any divisor `D ∈ Div(G) := Z^{V(G)}` of degree
    5820	`deg(D) = Σ_v D(v)`, the *rank* `r_G(D) := max\{k : ∀ E ∈ Div_+^k(G),
    5821	|D − E| ≠ ∅\}` (where `|D|` denotes the linear-equivalence class under
    5822	chip-firing moves and `Div_+^k` is the set of effective degree-`k`
    5823	divisors) satisfies `r_G(D) − r_G(K_G − D) = deg(D) + 1 − g(G)`, where
    5824	`g(G) = |E(G)| − |V(G)| + 1` is the cyclomatic genus and `K_G` is the
    5825	canonical divisor `K_G(v) = deg_G(v) − 2`. Question: define the
    5826	*arithmetic graph* `\Gamma_N := (V_N, E_N)` with `V_N = [2, N]` and
    5827	`E_N = \{(a, b) : a \mid b \text{ or } b \mid a, a \neq b\}` (the
    5828	divisibility graph), and the *prime divisor* `D_P^N \in Div(\Gamma_N)`
    5829	with `D_P^N(v) = 1` if `v` prime, `0` otherwise — so
    5830	`deg(D_P^N) = π(N) - 1`. Compute `r_{\Gamma_N}(D_P^N)` via the Baker-
    5831	Norine algorithm (chip-firing reduction to the `q`-reduced divisor).
    5832	Does `r_{\Gamma_N}(D_P^N)` deviate by `> 5σ` from a matched-degree
    5833	random divisor `D_R^N` (place `π(N)` chips uniformly at random on
    5834	non-leaf vertices)?
    5835	
    5836	**Why frontier:** the *graph-divisorial rank* `r_G(D)` is a *non-linear*
    5837	combinatorial invariant — it does not factor through the Laplacian
