    5684	
    5685	**Question:** Mazur (1966) proposed the analogy "primes in `Spec(Z)`
    5686	↔ knots in `S^3`" and identified the *arithmetic linking number*
    5687	`lk(p, q) := \frac{1 - (p/q)}{2} \in \mathbb{F}_2` (the Legendre
    5688	symbol viewed as a `\mathbb{F}_2`-cocycle on the étale fundamental
    5689	group). Morishita 2002 *Crelle* 550, 141 extended this to higher
    5690	*arithmetic Milnor / Massey products*: the triple Massey product
    5691	`\langle p, q, r \rangle_2 \in \mathbb{F}_2` evaluates to the Rédei
    5692	symbol `[p, q, r]` (Rédei 1939), defined for prime triples with
    5693	all pairwise Legendre symbols `+1` (the "admissible" Borromean
    5694	condition). The Rédei symbol detects whether the triple is
    5695	*Borromean*: pairwise unlinked but jointly linked, like the (13, 61,
    5696	937) example with all Legendre symbols `+1` but Rédei symbol `-1`.
    5697	Question: is the empirical distribution of `[p, q, r]` on admissible
