    | §L1 NOVELTY_CHALLENGES — Leading-row + dead-col upper-triangulation for E2.1 orthogonal corner `(W, d=j+1)`: which W ≤ 72 admit a Lean-tractable triangulation with rows ⊂ [0, W) and R = φ(W)+1 ≤ 22? | EXHAUSTED | C | Comprehensive enumeration via DP-based bitmask reachability on column subsets (script: `experiments/formalisations/E2_1_mps_bond_dim/leading_row_search.py`). For each W, build row signatures `S(r) ⊆ {chosen R cols}` as bitmasks; DP over T ⊆ R-cols to decide if some col ordering admits row assignment with first-σ-position ∈ A_i nonempty for every i. **Outcome**: leading-row family closes **EXACTLY** `W ∈ {2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 18, 20}` and is structurally obstructed for every other W in `[2, 72]` with `R ≤ 22`. Obstructed set: `{7, 9, 11, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 19, 21, 22, 24, 25, 26, 27, 28, 30, 32, 33, 34, 36, 38, 40, 42, 44, 48, 50, 54, 60, 66}`. **W=10 correction**: previously listed as obstructed in S128/S129 RESEARCH_AGENDA notes ("multiplicity-2 residue pattern"), the S144 DP found the missing triangulation `ρ ↦ (1, 0, 4, 3, 9)`, `σ ↦ (8, 1, 2, 0, 6)` (diagonal primes `{19, 2, 43, 31, 97}`), giving an eleventh unconditional `mps_bond_dim` instance. **Mechanism for exhaustion**: a leading-row triangulation of an `R × R` 0/1 sub-matrix with `R = φ(W) + 1` requires that for some col ordering `σ`, the row `bottom-row` (= row at position `R`) has exactly one prime-position in the chosen R cols. For W with `R ≥ 7` and composite structure {prime power × small prime}, no such "isolated diagonal hit" exists in rows `[0, W)` because chiP windows of length W cluster primes by residue class. The DP is sufficient (true negation): `reach[2^R - 1] = false` ⇔ no triangulation exists. **Closes**: routes A^{(N)} for N ≥ 12 are ruled out at this parameter range; further single-session corner closures must use either (a) `Matrix.det_of_blockTriangular` for non-triangulizable matrices (multi-session), or (b) cofactor-expansion-based determinant proofs (e.g., the W=9 7×7 sub-matrix has det = 1 by row cofactor expansion but no row+col upper-triangulation; ~250 Lean lines per such corner). **Adds EDGE (negative shape, in EDGES.md as a refinement of E2.1)**: leading-row + dead-col triangulation closes E2.1 orthogonal corner exactly for `W ∈ {2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 18, 20}` at `R ≤ 22`. **Cross-domain ingredient**: bitmask DP over reachability (algorithmic, not number-theoretic). **Channelled mathematician**: none — purely combinatorial enumeration. Cites E2.1, references S98/S99/S106/S107/S117/S122/S128/S129/S137/S143/S144 (the closure chain). See `experiments/formalisations/E2_1_mps_bond_dim/leading_row_search.py` and `experiments/formalisations/E2_1_mps_bond_dim/leading_row_search_results.txt`, `archive/sessions/session144_l1_lean_w10_corner_and_search.md`. | 144 |
    | §D5 ATTACK_VECTORS — Continuous-time quantum walk on the divisor / coprime graph: does U(t) = exp(−iH t) with seed `|1⟩` and target `v_p = (1/√π(x)) Σ_{p≤x} |p⟩` concentrate amplitude polylogarithmically on primes (Childs glued-tree analogue)? (cross-domain: Childs 2009 PRL 102 = arXiv:0806.1972 + Childs-Cleve-Deotto-Farhi-Gutmann-Spielman 2003 STOC = arXiv:quant-ph/0209131) | FAIL | E | Frontier wild_swing S141 on the natural CTQW successor to D4 (S80, Szegedy closed E). H_G ∈ {A, L = D − A} on G ∈ {D_x, C_x}. Eigendecomposition U(t) = Σ_k e^{−iλ_k t} u_k u_k^T; amplitude `P(t) = |⟨v_p|U(t)|1⟩|²` swept on t ∈ [0, 500] at 5001 grid points. **Pre-registered falsifiers**: F-A classical equilibration baseline `π(x)/x` (sanity); F-B peak amplitude beats Cramér + odd-parity matched control by a factor that grows with x (A-grade); F-C isolated band-edge eigenvector with O(1) overlap with v_p (glued-tree A-grade signature); F-D closure mode confirmed across both Hamiltonian variants. **Outcome**: F-A passes, F-B fails (excess +4–5σ but BOUNDED and not scaling), F-C fails (top overlap decays as `x^{−0.20}`, no isolated cluster), F-D confirms across all 4 variants. **Scaling (divisor + H=A, x ∈ {32, 64, 96, 128, 192, 256, 384, 512, 768}, T=500)**: ratio_max(x) := max_t P(t) / (π(x)/x) ∈ {1.24, 1.34, 1.39, 1.30, 1.23, 1.29, 1.31, 1.13, 1.22}; OLS fit `1.151 + 0.609/log(x)` → x→∞ asymptote ≈ **1.151** (bounded constant). top_overlap(x) := max_k |⟨u_k|v_p⟩| ∈ {0.626, 0.532, 0.469, 0.455, 0.420, 0.393, 0.369, 0.352, 0.328}; OLS log-log fit `1.214 · x^{−0.200}` (slow polynomial decay, NOT constant). **C2 control (Cramér + odd parity, 100 seeds)**: z_peak = +5.4, +3.3, +5.1 at x = 64, 128, 256; z_mean = +4.6, +4.1, +4.0 — modest persistent excess (~+4σ residual) but does NOT scale. C1 (uniform random subset) z = +2.9, +3.9, +7.5, +10.2 grows but smaller than C3. C3 (random ER graph, same mean degree) z = +10.6, +22.1, +39.9, +65.8 — divisor graph IS structured, but structure